# Trivy ignore file — JUSTIFIED, TIME-WINDOWED exceptions only.
#
# Policy (Phase 226): no blanket ignores. Every entry must state (a) why it
# cannot be patched now, (b) why it is not exploitable in our images, and carry
# an `exp:` expiry date that forces re-review. Anything with an available fix is
# patched at build time via `apt-get/apk upgrade`, NOT ignored here.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CVE-2026-42496 (CRITICAL) / CVE-2026-42497 (HIGH) — perl-archive-tar path
# traversal (Archive::Tar < 3.08), present in perl-base on the python:3.14-slim
# base image (analytics, tarpit).
#   * No fix available: Debian trixie marks it `fix_deferred` — there is no
#     patched perl-base to upgrade to as of 2026-06-06.
#   * Not exploitable here: our images never invoke Archive::Tar to extract
#     untrusted archives; perl-base is only a transitive base-image package.
#   * Exit plan: Phase 229 (base-image consolidation) may move these images to a
#     perl-free base; otherwise re-review when Debian ships a fix.
CVE-2026-42496 exp:2026-09-04
CVE-2026-42497 exp:2026-09-04
